DESCRIPTION:If you haven’t heard of Lace Larrabee\, you will soon. Lace 
 is a nationally touring comedian\, actress\, and host whose debut comedy a
 lbum\, White Trash Cinderella\, produced by 800 Pound Gorilla Records\, se
 aled the number one spot on the comedy charts. The accompanying YouTube sp
 ecial amassed over 1.9 million views and counting. A former southern beaut
 y queen\, Lace ditched the pageants but kept her dominant stage presence\,
  unrivaled timing and trademark sass. As a season 17 semifinalist on Ameri
 ca’s Got Talent\, America loved her charming wit so much\, NBC brought h
 er back to roast Simon Cowell alongside Roastmaster General himself\, Jeff
  Ross. Lace turned her appearance on AGT into a Vegas residency as host of
  America’s Got Talent Superstars Live. For over 13 years\, Lace has been
  honing her self-deprecating humor and hilarious personal anecdotes into a
  style that is fiercely her own. Lace can captivate a room and garner laug
 hs as big as her personality.  From tales of growing up in a trailer to r
 elatable observations on friends\, family\, love and aging\, Lace turns li
 fe’s humiliating moments into an indomitable act of comedy. Lace’s can
 dor\, perspicacity\, and refreshingly real takes on life make comedians wa
 nt to be her\, audiences want to be best friends with her. Lace is a regul
 ar favorite on Sirius XM. Lace’s charisma radiates and her writing and d
 elivery are undeniable. Lace has found her voice and is passionate about e
 mpowering others to find and use theirs too through founding Atlanta's #1 
 comedy class\, Laugh Lab .
LOCATION:The Comedy Attic\, 123 S Walnut Street\, Bloomington\, IN
URL:https://www.comedyattic.com/shows/385673
X-SOURCE:The Comedy Attic
END:VEVENT
